ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57, D-94): layers laid over their parents directly when source-over
Library: resvg 0.48.1
Fixes: none (speed: tiny-skia draws every pixmap through its high-precision pipeline)
Upstream: none yet: to be proposed to tiny-skia (a low-precision path for an untransformed pixmap) or resvg (ours)
Remove when: tiny-skia draws an untransformed source-over pixmap without its high-precision pipeline, or resvg composites layers so, or this patch no longer applies

render::composite() lays a source-over layer onto its parent with its opacity directly (premultiplied,
rounded to the nearest level), any other blend mode through tiny-skia as before: draw_pixmap took half
the time of a document of large layers. The rounding differs from tiny-skia's by at most 3 levels.
Requires the three patches before it.

